  "id": "DrugBank_DB00997 - MONDO_16249",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is associated with Hereditary Site-specific Ovarian Cancer Syndrome through a chain of indications involving chemotherapy agents. The evidence suggests that Doxorubicin, when used in combination with cisplatin, paclitaxel, or carboplatin, may contribute to the development of this syndrome. These chemotherapeutic agents are linked to the syndrome through their roles in treating cancers such as ovarian mucinous adenocarcinoma, Kaposi's sarcoma, and clear cell adenocarcinoma. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the shared association with chemotherapy regimens implies a potential role of these agents in the pathogenesis of the syndrome. The evidence highlights a recurring pattern of chemotherapeutic use linked to the syndrome, suggesting a possible mechanistic link between chemotherapy exposure and the development of site-specific ovarian cancer. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of chemotherapeutic agents in the context of hereditary ovarian cancer syndromes.",
